module contract;

// Card W45-CONTRACT-REVISION-MODE: every contract in this module is
// `revision flexible` (contract spec C06.2): it binds by name and declared
// signature at any revision of the audited project, and reports list the libc
// contracts as one standing assumption, the libc/C-standard ABI premise. The
// C library's version stays in the build's provenance.

// POSIX mutex acquire/release — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card CONSTRUCTOR-RESIDUALS-ABI-TYPEDEF. This module declares TRUSTED
// ASSUMPTIONS about two C library functions. It verifies nothing: no C body is
// analyzed by this loader, and a declaration is a premise.
//
// ## Read from the declaration in the analysed unit
//
//   extern int pthread_mutex_lock (pthread_mutex_t *__mutex)
//     __THROWNL __nonnull ((1));
//   extern int pthread_mutex_unlock (pthread_mutex_t *__mutex)
//     __THROWNL __nonnull ((1));
//
// (`/usr/include/pthread.h:794` and `:835` on the audited host.) Both take one
// `pthread_mutex_t *` and return `int`.
//
//   * `pthread_mutex_t` is `typedef union { … } pthread_mutex_t;`
//     (`/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu/bits/pthreadtypes.h:67-72`) — an aggregate
//     the typedef DEFINES rather than names. Card LOADER-ABI's reader would not
//     commit to it and withdrew both declarations at every call site
//     (`abi-unreadable-declaration`); this card's widening reads it, and a
//     pointer to it is the same opaque `ptr<mut, u8>` projection every other
//     object pointer has.
//   * `__THROWNL` and `__nonnull ((1))` expand to `__attribute__` suffixes,
//     which carry no type and which the ABI reader steps over.
//
// ## The custody statement, and only it
//
// Neither function allocates, frees, reallocates or takes custody of the mutex
// object. The caller owns the storage on both sides of either call, so the
// caller's obligations are unchanged: that is exactly `resource_borrowed`, and
// an `int` return is `resource_return_none()`.
//
// ## What this says nothing about
//
// Nothing about mutual exclusion, lock ordering, deadlock, recursion, error
// returns (`EDEADLK`, `EOWNERDEAD`, `EINVAL`), the initialised state of the
// mutex, or which data the mutex protects. QCore's checked-concurrency mutex
// model (`CheckedMutexInvariantV1`, `AGENTS.md` constraint 27) is a separate
// discipline over declared QCore source and is untouched by this declaration:
// this is a per-call custody statement about the CALLER's obligations on the
// pointed-to object, and nothing more.
//
// ## Portability, recorded rather than assumed
//
// These are the POSIX spellings. On a host whose analysed units do not declare
// them, this module names functions no unit contains and is inert text there —
// the same measured-inert situation card PROD-CONTRACTS recorded for
// `flb_trace`, and harmless for the same reason.

extern fn pthread_mutex_lock(mutex: ptr<mut, u8>) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(mutex);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

extern fn pthread_mutex_unlock(mutex: ptr<mut, u8>) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    requires resource_revision(flexible);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(mutex);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
